}}'''Koshima za Amaterasu Mitama Shrine'' (Koshima za Amateru Mitama Jinja, Kijimaza Amaterasu Mitama Shrine) is {{ill|lt=Kyoto City|Q34600|qid=Q34600|1=Kyoto}}{{j alink|Ukyo-ku|Q580186}}{{ill|lt=Uzumasa|Q11444482|qid=Q11444482|1=Uzumasa}}{{ill|lt=Shrine|Q845945|qid=Q845945|1=Shinto shrine}} located in Morigahigashi-cho. It is {{ill|UNKNOWN|qid=Q134917286|lt=Shikiuchi|1=Shikinaisha|qid=Q134917286|lt=Shikinaisha}} ({{ill|lt=Meishin Taisha|Q9610964|qid=Q9610964|1=Myōjin Taisha}}), and {{ill|lt=Modern shrine rank system|Q712534|qid=Q712534|lt=Old shrine rank|1=Modern system of ranked Shinto shrines}} is {{ill|lt=Gosha|Q134917316|qid=Q134917316|1=Gō-sha}}.

It is also commonly known as ``Konoshima Shrine'' (Konoshima Shrine) and ``Kaikono Yashiro'' (Silkworm Shrine). This shrine has long been worshiped as the god of prayers for rain, and is known for having a rare {{ill|lt=three-pillar torii|Q3532297|qid=Q3532297|1=Mihashira Torii}} within its grounds.

=== Enshrined God ===
The following five deities are enshrined. </ref>.
:* {{ill|lt=Amenominakanushikami|Q2842779|qid=Q2842779|1=Ame-no-Minakanushi}}
:* {{ill|UNKNOWN|lt=Okuni Tamakami|1=UNKNOWN}}
